        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "3beba9b8-c329-5d93-b0d2-e94e0c696c59",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Chinese Chongqing Dog, Kanni, Tugou, Chinese Field Dog, Xiasi Dog\n- Places: China, Tamil Nadu, Zami River, Kyondaw, Phadaw, Apalon, Kanni, Danon, Kyain Seikgyi, Chaunghanakwa, Mon State\n- Concepts: hunting, family protection, coursing game, indigenous sighthound breeds\n\nFacts:\n- The Chinese Chongqing Dog was used in its early years for hunting wild boar and rabbits.\n- The Chinese Chongqing Dog is now used in China to protect families and belongings.\n- The Kanni is a rare indigenous South Indian sighthound breed of dog found in Tamil Nadu.\n- The name Kanni means maiden.\n- The Kanni breed is used mainly for coursing game.\n- Tugou includes the Chinese Field Dog, the Chinese Chongqing Dog, the Xiasi Dog, and several other native dog breeds distributed across China.\n- The Zami River flows north past Kyondaw, Phadaw, Apalon, Kanni, Danon, Kyain Seikgyi, and Chaunghanakwa, where it flows into Mon State.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "9ded8051-c2fc-5301-9f9f-3d0402b14f9d",
        "text": "Page: Chinese Chongqing Dog. Sentence: In its early years, it was used for hunting wild boar and rabbits, but it's now used in China to protect families and belongings.\nPage: Kanni. Sentence: The Kanni, which means maiden, is a rare indigenous South Indian sighthound breed of dog found in the state of Tamil Nadu.\nPage: Kanni. Sentence: The breed is used mainly for coursing game.\nPage: Tugou. Sentence: Tugou includes the most popular Chinese dog breed - the Chinese Field Dog (, pinyin: \"zhōng huá tián yuán quǎn\"), Chinese Chongqing Dog, Xiasi Dog, and several other native dog breeds distributed across China.\nPage: Zami River. Sentence: It flows north past Kyondaw, Phadaw, Apalon, Kanni, Danon, Kyain Seikgyi and Chaunghanakwa, where it flows into Mon State.",
        "type": "DocumentChunk"
